OFFSET  TYPE     LENGTH  DESCRIPTION                                     FLAGS
==============================================================================
 0000   BYTE       01    ARCHIVER FLAGS (SEE BELOW)                        (B)
 0001   STRING     05    ARCHIVE EXTENSION FOR IDENTIFICATION              (U)
 0007   STRING     20    ARCHIVER NAME                                     (-)
 0028   STRING     79    ARCHIVE TEST COMMAND                              (-)
 0108   STRING     79    ARCHIVE FILE_ID.DIZ EXTRACT COMMAND               (-)
 0188   STRING     79    ARCHIVE FILE_ID.DIZ ADD COMMAND                   (-)
 0268   STRING     79    ARCHIVE VIEW COMMAND                              (-)
 0348   STRING     15    KEYWORD FOR "ARCHIVE CORRUPTED" #1                (-)
 0364   STRING     15    KEYWORD FOR "ARCHIVE CORRUPTED" #2                (-)
 0380   STRING     15    KEYWORD FOR "ARCHIVE CORRUPTED" #3                (-)
 0396   BYTE       01    MIN LEVEL REQUIRED TO VIEW                        (-)
 0397   FREE BLOCK 03    FREE SPACE FOR FUTURE DEVELOPMENT                 (-)
 0400   END        00    TOTAL LENGTH: 400 BYTES                           (-)
==============================================================================

1) ALL STRINGS ARE NULL-TERMINATED. FIELD LENGTHS DO NOT CONTAIN THE NULLBYTE


BIT   DESCRIPTION                                               ARCHIVER FLAGS
==============================================================================
 0    0: FILE ARCHIVER                 1: DISK ARCHIVER
 1    0: USE ONLINE CHECKING           1: USE OFFLINE CHECKING
 2    0: DON'T GET DATE FROM DIZ       1: GET DATE FROM FILE_ID.DIZ
 3    0: DON'T DELETE IF CORRUPT       1: DELETE IF CORRUPT
 4    0: DON'T DISPLAY ARCHIVER OUTPUT 1: DISPLAY ARCHIVER OUTPUT
